    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d815">

                <pb facs="0695" n="619" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg619"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.11/8274</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Vice Consul Blocker to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1097</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Eagle Pass</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-12-07">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 7, 1916</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: * * * Enclosed is an original [manifesto]
                    to the people of Mexico, signed by General Villa, at San Andres, Chihuahua,
                    setting forth the platform of Villa and his colleagues.</p>
                <p>It seems evident that General Murguia, the Government commander, successfully
                    reached Chihuahua and wrested it from the hands of the bandits, but on the other
                    hand he has left a wide strip of territory between Torreon, his former base, and
                    the capital city of Chihuahua. It also seems that his advance north did not
                    cover any territory except along the Mexican Central Railroad and the town of
                    Parral is still under control of the bandits.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">William P. Blocker</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d815-a1.xml" xpointer="d815-a1"/>
            </div>
